Announcement was made of a Public Hearing to be held October 25, 2010 at 6:00 p.m. in
City Council Chambers for a transfer of ownership for a restaurant liquor license application
filed with the City Clerk’s Office for Soo Hyun Choi, LLC d/b/a Tokyo Bowl, 1829 Dell Range
Boulevard, Cheyenne, WY. (License currently held by Iron Chefs, Inc. d/b/a Tokyo Bowl, 1829
Dell Range Boulevard, Cheyenne, WY.)

Announcement was made of the appointment of Michael Godown to the Tourism
Promotion Joint Powers Board, and Tim Thorson to the City-County Health Board, to be
confirmed October 25, 2010.  Under other business and upon inquiry relative to whether Mr.
Thorson, a candidate running for an elected position involving the Board’s jurisdiction, would be
able to serve on the Board if elected, Mayor Kaysen expressed his belief that, if elected, the
individual may need to resign from the Board.
Announcement was made of the appointment of Kadi Davis, Ian Dome, Jay Egan-
Wright, Karolyn Hopfensperger, Dean Jackson, John Matsen, Bobby McGarry, Monica Mencer,
McKinzea Olsen, Jacob Peterson Gary Sayler, Isaiah Sims, Josh Walker, and  Sabrina Westover
to the Mayor’s Youth Council, to be confirmed October 25, 2010.
Under other business:
 Amy Threewitt, commented on the loss of a downtown grocery store since the Safeway
Store was sold and the burden to low income and elderly individuals who live in the area who
depended on the store.  She requested review of a possible direct transit bus route to grocery
stores on Saturdays.  James Perot McNeil agreed with the need to have a downtown grocery
store and noted his property concerns in the downtown area.  Jan Nelson-Schroll questioned
whether there were any initiatives or pending information on efforts toward another grocery
store in the downtown area.  Mayor Kaysen advised staff has been in communications with
parties interested in the topic and that review will be made with regard to transit bus services to
grocery stores on Saturdays, stating there is currently a daily route to grocery stores during the
week.  Comment was made in support of transit services to groceries stores on a regular basis.
